        "original_id": "7b58609b-2648-57c8-86cf-cff4e0f27959",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Friedrich Ratzel\n- Concepts: Lebensraum\n- Organizations: Nazi Party, Nazi Germany\n- Events: World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Friedrich Ratzel was a German geographer and ethnographer who lived from August 30, 1844 to August 9, 1904.\n- Friedrich Ratzel was notable for first using the term \"Lebensraum\" (\"living space\") in the sense later used by the National Socialists.\n- The Nazi Party and Nazi Germany supported the most extreme form of the Lebensraum ideology until the end of World War II.",
